# Upstream FSST's fsst_decompress() writes symbols with
#   #define FSST_UNALIGNED_STORE(dst,src) memcpy((unsigned long long*)(dst), &(src), 8)
# The memcpy itself is byte-wise and safe, but the cast of an unaligned
# destination to unsigned long long* is formally undefined, and UBSan reports it
# ten times (once per expansion in the little-endian fast path and its Duff's
# device). It is upstream code, deliberately unaligned -- FSST even ships
# -DFSST_MUST_ALIGN for platforms that cannot take it -- so this experiment
# suppresses the check for third_party rather than patching the snapshot.
# Verified: with these suppressions the sanitizer run is completely clean, so
# every remaining report would belong to this experiment's own code.
alignment:*third_party/fsst/*
